16 0 obj
<</A 69 0 R/Alt(\(a\) Aerial view of farmland with a red outline marking a section. \(b\) A field with plants and netting supported by wooden poles, with power lines in the background. \(c\) A pathway through a green field edged by bushes. \(d\) Close-up of unripe blueberries. \(e\) Partially ripe blueberries turning pink. \(f\) Ripe blueberries with a blue hue.)/K 1/P 8 0 R/Pg 47 0 R/S/Figure/T()>>
endobj

17 0 obj
<</A 70 0 R/Alt(Blueberry plant with clusters of leaves and three stages of berry development highlighted: immature \(green\), semi-mature \(purple\), and mature \(blue\). Each stage is marked with red arrows pointing to insets showing the berries' close-up views.)/K 0/P 8 0 R/Pg 47 0 R/S/Figure/T()>>
endobj

18 0 obj
<</A 71 0 R/Alt(Flowchart depicting a neural network architecture with three sections: Backbone, Neck, and Head. Backbone includes layers labeled C2f and CBS, processing the input. Neck features SPPF, multiple Upsample layers, concatenations, and C2f layers. Head contains a Detect layer leading to output. Elements like Concat and CBS are annotated for clarity.)/K 0/P 8 0 R/Pg 49 0 R/S/Figure/T()>>
endobj

19 0 obj
<</A 72 0 R/Alt(Flowchart of a neural network architecture divided into three sections: Backbone, Neck, and Head. The Backbone includes alternating AEF and CBS blocks processing inputs. The Neck features SPPF, Upsample, DSAA, CBS, and CGDS modules interconnected with C nodes for concatenation. The Head has an SDCH module leading to the output. Lines indicate data flow paths between modules.)/K 0/P 8 0 R/Pg 50 0 R/S/Figure/T()>>
endobj

20 0 obj
<</A 73 0 R/Alt(Diagram showing three sections: \(a\) DSAA, \(b\) CATM, \(c\) CGLU. \(a\) DSAA includes PWC and DWC layers, followed by CATM, then CGLU. \(b\) CATM involves operations on Y, producing Q, K, V, achieving spatial and channel adjustments, resulting in Z. \(c\) CGLU features a Z feedback loop, linear layers, DWC, culminating in an operation output. Each component is enclosed in dashed boxes.)/K 0/P 8 0 R/Pg 51 0 R/S/Figure/T()>>
endobj

21 0 obj
<</A 74 0 R/Alt(Flowchart illustrating an Adaptive Enhancement Framework \(AEF\) with Contour Attention. It shows an input image processed through Adaptive Average Pooling at varying sizes \(12x12, 9x9, 6x6, 3x3\). The pooled outputs lead to Pointwise Convolutions \(PWC\), followed by Depthwise Convolutions \(DWC\) and Contour Attention, with elements like sigmoid functions and upsampling involved, merging into a final output.)/K 0/P 8 0 R/Pg 52 0 R/S/Figure/T()>>
endobj

22 0 obj
<</A 75 0 R/Alt(Flowchart illustrating a neural network architecture. Section \(a\) titled CGDS shows an input leading to parallel convolution paths, then merging through CBS and Conv layers, ending at output. Section \(b\) titled FC depicts a sequence of Linear, ReLU, Linear, and Sigmoid operations. Components include Conv, DConv, AdaptiveAvgPool2d, and connections through Fully Connected \(FC\) layers.)/K 1/P 8 0 R/Pg 53 0 R/S/Figure/T()>>
endobj

23 0 obj
<</A 76 0 R/Alt(Flowchart illustrating a network structure. Three input blocks labeled P3, P4, and P5 with sizes 80x80, 40x40, 20x20 each connect to modules labeled CGS. CGS leads to a module called DEConv, which outputs to two layers, Conv_Reg and Conv_Cls, followed by a Scale block. CGS consists of Conv, GroupNorm, and SiLU.)/K 0/P 8 0 R/Pg 53 0 R/S/Figure/T()>>
endobj

24 0 obj
<</A 77 0 R/Alt(Diagram of a process flow with five parallel paths. The top path includes a \215Vanilla Conv\216 block leading to a sum node. Below, four paths labeled \215CDC,\216 \215ADC,\216 \215HDC,\216 and \215VDC\216 also lead to the sum node, with a shared input and output on each side.)/K 0/P 8 0 R/Pg 54 0 R/S/Figure/T()>>
endobj

25 0 obj
<</A 78 0 R/Alt(Flowchart illustrating the ByteTrack process. A detection box inputs into classification, splitting into multiple classes \(class 1 to class n\). Each class undergoes a Kalman filter and then matching, resulting in a detection box with class and ID.)/K 0/P 8 0 R/Pg 55 0 R/S/Figure/T()>>
endobj

26 0 obj
<</A 79 0 R/Alt(Bar chart showing detection accuracy of various YOLO models for blueberry maturity levels: overall, mature, semi-mature, and immature. Each group of bars represents a model, with accuracy percentages on the vertical axis and models labeled on the horizontal axis. Colors distinguish maturity levels.)/K 0/P 8 0 R/Pg 56 0 R/S/Figure/T()>>
endobj

27 0 obj
<</A 80 0 R/Alt(Dense foliage is shown with several identified points marked in green and blue boxes, accompanied by labels such as \215ID:3240 green\216 and \215ID:3219 blue\216. A data overlay lists frame rate, processing FPS, total count, and other statistics.)/K 0/P 8 0 R/Pg 58 0 R/S/Figure/T()>>
endobj

28 0 obj
<</A 81 0 R/Alt(Three side-by-side images of dense green foliage with superimposed data text, including frame numbers, processing stats, and elapsed time. Green lines and boxes highlight areas on the leaves in each image.)/K 0/P 8 0 R/Pg 59 0 R/S/Figure/T()>>
endobj

29 0 obj
<</A 82 0 R/Alt(Bar chart comparing tracking algorithm performance \(mAPc\) across three videos and average. ByteTrack, represented in blue, scores highest across all categories. OCSORT in orange follows closely, while StrongSORT in green scores lowest. Scores: Video 1 - ByteTrack 69.07, OCSORT 67.73, StrongSORT 59.32; Video 2 - ByteTrack 74.94, OCSORT 77.75, StrongSORT 24.30; Video 3 - ByteTrack 73.45, OCSORT 70.76, StrongSORT 37.32; Average - ByteTrack 72.49, OCSORT 72.08, StrongSORT 40.31.)/K 0/P 8 0 R/Pg 60 0 R/S/Figure/T()>>
endobj

30 0 obj
<</A 83 0 R/Alt(Close-up of blueberries on a branch, some blue and some unripe green. A peach hanging on a tree with green leaves. Unripe strawberries transitioning to red, hanging from a plant above a gray background.)/K 0/P 8 0 R/Pg 61 0 R/S/Figure/T()>>
endobj

31 0 obj
<</A 84 0 R/Alt(Heatmap comparing YOLO detection models YOLOv8, YOLOv9, YOLOv10, YOLOv11, and STF-YOLO across different object categories from the VOC2007 dataset. Color intensity represents mAP at 0.5 thresholds, with values ranging from 0.416 to 0.831. Darker blue indicates higher mAP scores, while lighter colors show lower scores.)/K 0/P 8 0 R/Pg 62 0 R/S/Figure/T()>>
endobj

32 0 obj
<</A 85 0 R/Alt(Comparison of YOLO model versions \(v8, v9, v10, YOLO-SDFM, MAF-YOLO, STF-YOLO\) detecting colors and confidence scores in a leafy environment. Each model version shows variations in detecting \215blue\216 and \215green\216 with associated scores, highlighting differences in accuracy and precision across the models. STF-YOLO includes zoomed-in insets to show detail in detection comparisons.)/K 1/P 8 0 R/Pg 64 0 R/S/Figure/T()>>
endobj

33 0 obj
<</A 86 0 R/Alt(Comparison of plant detection results using different YOLO models, including YOLOv8, YOLOv9, YOLOv10, YOLO-SDFM, MAF-YOLO, and STF-YOLO. Each model's detection is marked with colored labels and confidence scores, displaying differences in accuracy and recognition. STF-YOLO highlights detected objects with red rectangles and enlarged views for precision inspection.)/K 0/P 8 0 R/Pg 64 0 R/S/Figure/T()>>
endobj

34 0 obj
<</A 87 0 R/Alt(Image showing a series of deep learning model comparisons for fruit detection. Six models, YOLO versions eight through STF-YOLO, display identifications of blueberry and leaf regions with colored bounding boxes and confidence scores. Differences in detection are highlighted through various arrangements of blue, green, and red boxes, alongside text labels indicating the fruit color determined by each model, such as \215blue\216 or \215purple.")/K 1/P 8 0 R/Pg 65 0 R/S/Figure/T()>>
endobj

35 0 obj
<</A 88 0 R/Alt(Two images labeled as \(a\) and \(b\) show dense green foliage. Each image has highlighted areas zoomed in on berries, with annotations indicating color intensity. Image \(a\) includes a berry with a blue intensity of 0.81, while image \(b\) features berries with blue intensity values of 0.82 and 0.35, as well as green intensity values of 0.80, 0.56, and 0.59.)/K 0/P 8 0 R/Pg 65 0 R/S/Figure/T()>>
endobj

36 0 obj
<</A 89 0 R/Alt(Blueberries on a bush are shown in three rows representing different ripeness stages labeled as Minor, Moderate, and Severe. Each row contains four images displaying variations in berry color and leaf coverage.)/K 0/P 8 0 R/Pg 66 0 R/S/Figure/T()>>
endobj

